  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "yjw8qb",
   "en": "As Iran the first thing you want to do is begin justifying on Iraq so you can get more resources for when you reform the Persian Empire. Once you take out Iraq you can turn your focus onto Afghanistan and take them over too. Now from here on out you will need to declare war on France and Britain so prepare your forces on the borders of their colonies and attack them. You will need Syria, Jordan, and Pakistan in order to do this. After you've preferably peaced out the European Powers you can go and invade Turkey. They shouldn't pose much of a threat to you at this point as your army should be large. Once you've taken Turkey you can take Greece if you feel like it but now you've basically reformed the Persian Empire! You are probably a great power by now so taking over the world should be easy from here."
  },
  {
   "k": "1teaf1q",
   "en": "If you don't feel lucky and want to play it safe, the best option will be to become communist and join the Soviet Union as soon as possible, since you share borders with it, enjoying its protection will guarantee your survival, if you have time, try to take Iraq for it's manpower and resources once you have joined the Comintern, it will be easier with Soviet help, still try to take Afghanistan if you still have time, make sure you help as much as possible in the soviet wars to get military experience and improve your units, at the same time focus on the navy so you can defend the Persian gulf and fortify the border with the British Raj since the UK has approaches to declare war on Iran and will most likely call the Raj to war since they share a border."
  },
